{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01163",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.21,
      "end_seconds": 6.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Mm, um, hi doctor, am I too early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.58,
      "end_seconds": 11.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.35,
      "end_seconds": 19.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.58,
      "end_seconds": 30.94,
      "duration_seconds": 10.36,
      "text": "Mainly I've been passing a lot of urine. That's why I came. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.19,
      "end_seconds": 34.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.63,
      "end_seconds": 41.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so about three days, give or take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 43.24,
      "end_seconds": 48.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Okay, so I think it's been nearer five days, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.89,
      "end_seconds": 54.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to five days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.24,
      "end_seconds": 58.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Actually, yes, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.13,
      "end_seconds": 63.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "right, how much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.57,
      "end_seconds": 80.28,
      "duration_seconds": 14.71,
      "text": "I'd call it moderate. I've also had being very thirsty, since yesterday. Let me think, there's deep fast breathing as well. Oh, and vomiting"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.12,
      "end_seconds": 83.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Has there been any cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.19,
      "end_seconds": 85.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "No cough, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 86.73,
      "end_seconds": 92.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice cough. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.37,
      "end_seconds": 101.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "Oh, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.27,
      "end_seconds": 109.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. How about chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.0,
      "end_seconds": 113.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "no, uh, no chest pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.28,
      "end_seconds": 118.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Alright, how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.51,
      "end_seconds": 121.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.07,
      "end_seconds": 125.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.98,
      "end_seconds": 130.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Oh, I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.24,
      "end_seconds": 146.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.31,
      "end_seconds": 152.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.57,
      "end_seconds": 157.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.87,
      "end_seconds": 164.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.9,
      "end_seconds": 168.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.23,
      "end_seconds": 173.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.64,
      "end_seconds": 177.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.84,
      "end_seconds": 181.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.57,
      "end_seconds": 195.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.82,
      "end_seconds": 218.31,
      "duration_seconds": 21.49,
      "text": "I, I take gliclazide, 80 milligrams, twice a day. I take alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week. Spironolactone. I take it 25 milligrams, once a day. Actually, I used to take carvedilol, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.22,
      "end_seconds": 221.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Right, what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.49,
      "end_seconds": 246.15,
      "duration_seconds": 23.66,
      "text": "I've had diabetes, yes. Ah, I've had thin bones, yes. My neighbour said I should get it looked at. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. Um, yes, heart failure. It's the not knowing that gets to me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.01,
      "end_seconds": 251.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.56,
      "end_seconds": 258.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Oh, yes, plasters, it gives me a red itchy rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.93,
      "end_seconds": 271.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.05,
      "end_seconds": 283.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.36,
      "end_seconds": 307.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "okay: blood pressure 132 over 81, SpO2 97 percent on room air, pulse 120."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.77,
      "end_seconds": 311.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "ah, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.67,
      "end_seconds": 314.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "We'll go over that shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.58,
      "end_seconds": 322.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.04,
      "end_seconds": 325.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "yes, that's fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.72,
      "end_seconds": 329.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.27,
      "end_seconds": 351.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "you are dry, breathing deeply and your breath smells fruity"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.91,
      "end_seconds": 366.03,
      "duration_seconds": 11.12,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Putting it all together, it's hard to say. Diabetic ketoacidosis is one possibility and a severe infection another, and I'd rather not commit yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 369.38,
      "end_seconds": 373.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Erm, I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.96,
      "end_seconds": 401.87,
      "duration_seconds": 26.91,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like diabetic ketoacidosis, but I'd like to confirm. I'd like to arrange blood gas and electrolytes for DKA. Let's book a blood sugar and ketone test to look into thirst and vomiting. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. You need to go to hospital now for insulin and fluids."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.94,
      "end_seconds": 430.8,
      "duration_seconds": 26.86,
      "text": "Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. The emergency team would be the right next step, I'll refer you. Keep an eye out, and if you cannot get there now, call us the same day or go to emergency. Let's plan a check straight away. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 432.76,
      "end_seconds": 435.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Um, thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}